CLASS:: SwarmPartialPlotData
summary:: Project cached swarm snapshots into partial-plot records
categories:: Libraries>SwarmSynth
related:: Classes/SwarmMath, Classes/SwarmAuditionGUI

DESCRIPTION::
SwarmPartialPlotData is a pure projection helper. It does not evaluate synthesis callbacks, create views, or start audio. Plot interactions can therefore repeatedly project one controller-owned capture without resampling it.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: fromCapture
Returns an Event containing sorted plot records, axis limits, Nyquist information, filter choices, labels, and capture status.

argument:: capture
An Event or Dictionary with code::records:: from link::Classes/SwarmMath:: code::playbackSnapshot::, a symbolic code::name::, a positive code::sampleRate::, and optional labels and status.

The optional code::frequencyInterpretation:: callback receives each record's values and returns the numeric oscillator frequency represented by those values. This supports synth controls whose captured code::freq:: is a base parameter rather than the final oscillator input. code::defaultNyquistPolicy:: may be code::\none::, code::\fold::, code::\mute::, or code::\taper::. Both fields may be top-level or in a code::metadata:: dictionary. The defaults are direct code::freq:: interpretation and code::\none::.

argument:: axis
code::\frequency:: or code::\partial::.

argument:: display
code::\generated:: shows interpreted oscillator inputs. code::\policy:: applies the captured or inherited Nyquist policy.

argument:: baseIndex
Optional zero-based base-frequency filter.

argument:: variation
Optional zero-based variation filter.

EXAMPLES::

code::
~capture = (
    name: \example, sampleRate: 48000, status: \preview,
    defaultNyquistPolicy: \fold,
    records: ~state.playbackSnapshot(1234, true)
);
~plot = SwarmPartialPlotData.fromCapture(~capture, \frequency, \policy);
~plot.records.size.postln;
::
